# The real input file. This is the whole privacy design of this project in one line.
#
# people.json holds names, dates of birth, diagnoses and medication lists for real people, very
# often children. It is ignored before it exists, so that the first time somebody copies
# people.example.json across and fills it in, git already refuses to stage it. Adding the rule
# after the fact does not help: by then the record is in the history.
#
# people.example.json is committed and holds invented people only. scripts/privacy_scan.py
# fails if this rule is missing, if git check-ignore disagrees with it, if people.json is
# tracked anyway, or if anybody in the example file stops being visibly fictional.
people.json
people.*.json
!people.example.json

# Generated output. Cards built from a real people.json are just as sensitive as the input.
dist/
build/
docs/*.png

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*credentials*
*secret*
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.next/
